    "blurb": "The set builds to a peak with an epic Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven sequence, followed by a soulful Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s guitar shines front‑and‑center while Tom Constanten adds sweet organ texture; Good Lovin’ and Mason’s Children > High Time round out a solid early‑70 performance.",
    "review": "On January 17, 1970 the Grateful Dead delivered a winter‑70 showcase at Oregon State University that still feels fresh. The first half rolls through classic Americana—Dire Wolf, China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider and a rousing Good Lovin’—but it’s the second half that steals the show. A seamless Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven marathon showcases Jerry Garcia’s immaculate SG tone and fearless improvisation, with Phil Lesh locking into the rhythmic vortex. Tom Constanten (Pig) provides a funky, church‑sourced Hammond flavor that colors the jam, while the dual drummers keep the pulse tight. The night closes on a heartfelt Turn On Your Lovelight, leaving the audience humming long after the final chord.",
